think Eighth lap. The crypto arc now has sixteen parity-GREEN files, a per-file witness for each, and a whole-suite witness. The recommend named the front-door crux: a crypto/README.md index that names each primitive, its RFC/parity reference, and the suite witness — the highest-Lindy remaining crypto thread, since a README is read thousands of times over years and this one is how an auditor first meets the stack. It also feeds the docs-compression pass and the public seed.
think Design (self-approved): a Radiant front door under TAME framing — what the library is and why (audit honesty, no std.crypto, byte-for-byte parity vs RFC + Zig std.crypto, Monocypher the target not a copied line), the sixteen files in five dependency tiers as reference tables (hashes · ChaCha/Poly · field+curve · key agreement · compositions), the witness story (per-file + the one-command suite), and the honest horizons (constant-time timing-safety, Monocypher-source parity) plus the custody gate (keys stay the maintainer's hand). A README front door earns a radiant wish, per radiant-wishes-ending.md.
think docs-implementation-sync: every claim is checkable and checked — sixteen files (ls confirmed), each with a per-file witness (confirmed this loop), the suite witness GREEN across all sixteen (run this loop), the RFC references drawn from each file's own GREEN print. No behavioral claim written from memory.
